WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.467
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:06.167
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.234
What a great time to be in
New York City.

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:10.601
Fall in New York!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:12.868
There's nothing better.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.834
It's that special time when
all the vomit puddles

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:17.701
on the sidewalk go from
hard seltzer to hard cider.

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.901
You know what I'm saying?
It's very exciting.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.701
Well, guys,
everybody's talking about this.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.000
At a big Tesla event,

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Elon Musk unveiled the prototype
for a humanoid robot.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.267
Yeah, and the robot showed off
its human-like

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:30.501
walking skills when it entered.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:31.534
Watch this.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:41.567
Yeah. Yeah, that's great.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:43.767
[ Laughter ]
-What the...

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.467
-Billions of dollars
on a robot that walks like

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:46.667
it just ate Chipotle.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.100
It's like...
♪♪

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:58.300
-Guac extra.
-Some news from overseas.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.767
I heard that today
at the Vatican,

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:03.000
Pope Francis met
with Apple C.E.O. Tim Cook.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.000
I guess when you're the pope
and have tech issues,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.767
that's who they send.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.434
Meanwhile,
Adam and Eve were like,

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:10.868
"Oh, so now
we're cool with apples?

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.200
Interesting. Okay, good.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.534
Interesting."

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:17.701
I saw that Kim Kardashian
has agreed to pay a $1.3 million

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.934
fine for
promoting cryptocurrency

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.834
without saying
that she was being paid.

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.334
$1.3 million.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.200
Fining Kim Kardashian
$1.3 million

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.033
is like giving Elon Musk
a parking ticket.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:30.234
He's like, "Oh..."

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.334
I read that due to inflation,

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:35.133
single Americans
are going on fewer dates.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.534
You know it's bad when
your date says,

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.434
"This could have been a Zoom."

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.801
Yep, thanks to inflation,
single people are

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.033
going on fewer dates,
so to make up for it,

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:46.334
we're all going to go on a date
right now together.

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:48.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's time for "Togethering."

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:49.367
Here we go.

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:51.367
♪♪

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.901
I'm worried that
you're hotter than me.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:06.767
Uh, hi.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:09.267
I'll have
the second-cheapest wine.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.267
Thank you.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.501
Wow, this is
a very expensive restaurant.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.467
I might have
forgotten my wallet.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.434
I haven't decided yet.

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.200
Thanks.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.701
What's that?
Sure, we can split something.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:23.901
We'll split the soup.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:24.968
I'll have the upper half,

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.968
and you'll have the lower.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:29.801
Just so you know,

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:32.267
the bathroom was out of
toilet paper before I went.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:33.701
Just wanted...

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.701
How many siblings do you have?

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:40.567
Three? Me too!
Oh, my God! That's so crazy.

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:43.934
What's your middle name?

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:46.968
No, never mind. It's too soon.

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:49.067
Have you seen
"House of the Dragon"?

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:52.367
I haven't.
Why would I bring that up?

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:55.000
I wonder if I can
pull off a flirty wink.

00:02:57.501 --> 00:03:00.067
Nope, I can't.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.100
How many siblings do you have?

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.167
Oh, I already asked that one.

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.901
I'm going to get us
both out of this.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:06.567
I'm going get
an emergency work call

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:08.667
right now and never come back.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.634
-This has been...

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.634
-And, finally,
people are talking about this.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.267
At Paris Fashion Week,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.734
Bella Hadid
had her dress painted on.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:26.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
It was good, right?

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:27.267
Take a look at this.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.667
♪♪
Yeah.

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.067
Amazing.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.133
Yeah, when she walked
the runway, people didn't know

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.701
if she was a supermodel
or a Tesla robot.

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:40.801
We have a great show.

